I ate lunch at 2:15, in the library, from a vending machine, which I
want on the record as technically a meal. Platanitos and a ginger ale.
My mother would have called it a funeral for a lunch.
   The library is the old branch on the Concourse, the one with the
green-shaded lamps and the oak tables polished by about ninety years
of elbows. It’s the one place in the borough where being quiet is free,
and as established I can’t work in quiet. So I sat by the radiator, which
knocked, near a man who was snoring in a way I considered a public
service.
   My phone had been buzzing since noon.

   Sofía: that “is this anything” email
   Sofía: JC
   Sofía: where are you
   Sofía: ok i’m not waiting. it’s not spam. it’s so much worse than spam
   Sofía: are you in a hole. you’re in a hole aren’t you
   Sofía: i can see your location you absolute bobo. don’t move

One more text had come in under Sofía’s, from Denise at the arts space.

   Denise: Hi JC! Quick heads up, the board is holding your milestone payment until
   our partner review next week. Just process! Hope you’re well.




